# format=FAST
# Fusion MS-WB670 (SW 6.50, build 121) at source 51, controlled from a B&G Zeus
# SRX at source 39 over NMEA 2000, captured 2026-09-18 on a live bus.
#
# Shows that the zone field in the Fusion PGNs is ZERO-BASED, while the fixed
# four-slot status messages and the factory default names are one-based:
#
#   Zone Name index 0 = "Doghouse"   (the zone the UI calls Zone 1)
#   Zone Name index 1 = "Saloon"     (the zone the UI calls Zone 2)
#   Zone Name index 2 = "Zone 3"     (still on its factory default name)
#
# The operator then set the balance of "Saloon" to left 7 from the Zeus. The
# 126720 Set Balance command carries zone=1, and the 130820 Balance status
# answers with zone=1 value=-7 (negative = left).
#
# The nine 126720 Set Balance frames are the first non-zero-zone command frames
# captured from any controller; they decode via the fusionSetBalance variant
# added in #884, which was written from an MS-RA70N and had only zone 0 samples.
#
